simplescreenrecorder (0.3.3+GITe2e9336451-0librazik1) jessie; urgency=low

  * New upstream release:
    - v0.3.2:
      + Added Qt5 support (optional, Qt4 is still the default)
      + Added YUV422, YUV444 and RGB support (YUV420 is still the default)
      + Added pixelformat and sampleformat codec options.
      + Added benchmark.
      + Improved RTL support.
      + Bugfixes
    - v0.3.3:
      + Fixed mistake in configure.ac that was causing libssr-glinject.so to
        be linked with unwanted libraries.
    - Other adds since v0.3.3:
      + Add French, Swedish and Traditional Chinese translations.
      + Use pkg-config to find FFmpeg libraries.
      + Don't hold the lock while changing JACK connections.
      + Add man pages.
      + Add Keywords line to desktop file.
      + Don't refer to Qt 4 in about box (Qt 5 is supported too).
      + Fix --disable-x86-asm option.
  * Rebuild with pbuilder for LibraZiK (based on Debian Jessie).
  * debian/copyright:
    - add myself to the debian packaging copyright section.
    - rewrite this file to improve the machine-readable criteria.
  * debian/control:
    - check if the Homepage link is still valid. OK.
    - add mention to the LibraZiK project in "Description".
    - lists' style - one item per line.
    - update "Maintainer" and "Uploaders" Re: "debian-policy 5.6.2 and 5.6.3".
    - add "libpulse-dev" as a build dependency.
  * debian/patches/series:
    - add "desktop_file_l10n-FR.patch" (with dquilt).
  * debian/patches/desktop_file_l10n-FR.patch:
    - patch created (with dquilt) to add FR translation.
  * debian/rules:
    - enable pulseaudio by removing line 10 "	--disable-pulseaudio \".

